{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PZQxg3ZDjqZVyA4RFJ6PY5","type":"tool_result","content":"152:model Organization {\n153-  id        String   @id @default(uuid())\n154-  name      String\n155-  createdAt DateTime @default(now())\n156-  /// Documents spec 04 requirement 1 — the provider **new** envelopes are sent\n157-  /// through. Read once at the start of a send and pinned onto the envelope in the\n158-  /// transaction that flips it to `sent`; never read as authority afterwards. The\n159-  /// default is what makes every organization that predates the column keep the\n160-  /// in-house engine without a backfill.\n161-  signatureProviderKey   String    @default(\"internal\")\n162-  signatureProviderSetAt DateTime?\n163-  signatureProviderSetBy String?\n164-\n165-  signatureProviderSetByAccount Account? @relation(\"SignatureProviderSetBy\", fields: [signatureProviderSetBy], references: [id], onDelete: SetNull)\n166-\n167-  /// Requests spec 01 requirement 10 — atomically-allocated per-organization request\n168-  /// counter. Advanced inside a `SELECT ... FOR UPDATE` transaction on the organization\n169-  /// row before every Request insert, mirroring `Project.nextTaskNumber`. The default is\n170-  /// what makes a backfill unnecessary for organizations that predate the column.\n171-  nextRequestNumber Int @default(1)\n172-\n173-  memberships       Membership[]\n174-  documentTemplates DocumentTemplate[]\n175-  envelopes         Envelope[]\n176-  invitations       Invitation[]\n177-  projects          Project[]\n=== int tests use prisma? ===\n10:import { PrismaService } from '../src/prisma.service';\n48:    const membership = await prisma.membership.findUniqueOrThrow({ where: { accountId } });\n61:    const account = await prisma.account.create({\n71:    const membership = await prisma.membership.create({\n141:    await prisma.holiday.deleteMany();\n142:    await prisma.vacationRequest.deleteMany();\n143:    await prisma.vaca