",\n    \"The status=closed filter value and its expansion, on both the request list and the vacation section.\",\n    \"Request.topicId / Request.topicLabel and the topic member of every request response shape.\",\n    \"The Settings > Request topics screen, its modal, its audience switch and its reorder control - the DS has no primitive for either control (see dsGaps).\",\n    \"The About picker and its empty state on the new-request modal.\",\n    \"The requests list About column and topic filter.\",\n    \"manage-request-topics / ManageRequestTopics in both capability unions.\",\n    \"An integration route to 'an organization that predates the topics migration' - the harness applies every migration before any test runs, so this state has no way to exist (finding P2).\",\n    \"The reorder request contract - which row or rows a move writes, and what value the client sends (finding P1).\"\n  ],\n\n  \"testCases\": {\n    \"unit\": [\"TC-02-UNIT-01\", \"TC-02-UNIT-02\", \"TC-02-UNIT-03\", \"TC-02-UNIT-04\", \"TC-02-UNIT-05\", \"TC-02-UNIT-06\"],\n    \"int\": [\n      \"TC-02-INT-01\", \"TC-02-INT-02\", \"TC-02-INT-03\", \"TC-02-INT-04\", \"TC-02-INT-05\", \"TC-02-INT-06\",\n      \"TC-02-INT-07\", \"TC-02-INT-08\", \"TC-02-INT-09\", \"TC-02-INT-10\", \"TC-02-INT-11\", \"TC-02-INT-12\",\n      \"TC-02-INT-13\", \"TC-02-INT-14\", \"TC-02-INT-15\", \"TC-02-INT-16\", \"TC-02-INT-17\", \"TC-02-INT-18\",\n      \"TC-02-INT-19\", \"TC-02-INT-20\", \"TC-02-INT-21\"\n    ],\n    \"e2e\": [\"TC-02-E2E-01\", \"TC-02-E2E-02\", \"TC-02-E2E-03\", \"TC-02-E2E-04\", \"TC-02-E2E-05\", \"TC-02-E2E-06\"]\n  },\n\n  \"testIds\": [\n    \"settings-tab-request-topics\", \"request-topics-page\", \"request-topics-audience-staff\",\n    \"request-topics-audience-client\", \"request-topics-add-btn\", \"request-topic-row-{id}\",\n    \"request-topic-row-{id}-archive-btn\", \"request-topic-row-{id}-restore-btn\", \"request-topic-modal\",\n    \"request-topic-name\", \"request-topic-audience\", \"request-topic-type\", \"request-topic-submit\",\n    \"request-topic-error-name\", \"request-new-topic\", \"request-new-topic-empty\",\n    \"request-new-error-topic\", \"requests-topic-filter\", \"request-row-{id}-topic\",\n    \"request-detail-topic\", \"requests-new-btn\", \"request-new-modal\", \"request-new-submit\",\n    \"requests-status-filter\", \"request-row-{id}-status\", \"request-detail-status\", \"requests-page\"\n  ],\n\n  \"sections\": {\n    \"Summary\": \"no task - orientation; every rule it states is carried by a numbered requirement below it\",\n    \"Actors & Preconditions\": \"T3, T5 - the two capabilities the actors are defined by (manage-request-topics, create-request) are what the services check\",\n    \"Roles & Permission Matrix\": \"T1 (both capability unions and the matrix rows), T3 (the server check), T6 (the nav row)\",\n    \"Functional Requirements\": \"T1, T3, T4, T5, T6, T7 - every REQ-02-001..030 is named in a task's requirements\",\n    \"State Machine\": \"T3 - the four events and the FOR UPDATE invariant. The reorder event is BLOCKED by finding P1: no route in the Routes table can perform the multi-row write the Known Gaps table promises for it\",\n    \"Out of Scope\": \"no task - it names what is not built (per-topic fields, routing, SLAs, icons, usage counts, retiring accessKind from the database). T5 honours the last of these by leaving the column and its stored values untouched\",\n    \"Known Gaps\": \"no task for three of the four rows - they are accepted consequences. Row 4 (ordering) is finding P1\",\n    \"Acceptance Criteria\": \"T8 - each criterion's named observer is in testCases. AC-2's only observer is TC-02-INT-02, which is finding P2\",\n    \"Routes\": \"T3 (the five topic routes), T5 (the three amended request routes)\",\n    \"Error Messages\": \"T1 - see messages below\",\n    \"Status Labels\": \"T1 (the map and the filter expansion), T7 (the three surfaces that read it)\",\n    \"Data Model\": \"T2\",\n    \"Seed Data\": \"T2 (existing organizations), T4 (new ones) - one shared constant list\",\n    \"Validation Rules\": \"T1 (rules 1, 2, 4, 6, 7, 10), T3 (rules 3, 5), T5 (rules 8, 9)\",\n    \"Required data-testid Attributes\": \"T6, T7\",\n    \"Screens\": \"T6, T7\",\n    \"UI Description\": \"T6, T7\",\n    \"DS gaps\": \"T6 - see dsGaps\",\n    \"Edge Cases\": \"T3 (1, 11, 12, 13), T5 (2, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 15), T7 (3, 4, 13)\",\n    \"Security\": \"T3, T5 - guard chains, session-scoped queries, 404 for cross-organization on the topic routes and 400 topicUnavailable on create\",\n    \"Verification Plan\": \"T8 - every row marked 'created here' becomes a case that drives the real transition. The row for 'an organization that predates the topics migration' is finding P2\",\n    \"Test Cases\": \"T8\"\n  },\n\n  \"messages\": [\n    { \"context\": \"unknown audience on create or on the catalogue read\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_TOPIC_MESSAGES.audienceUnknown\", \"emittedBy\": \"apps/api/src/request-topics/request-topics.service.ts#createTopic, #listTopics\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"audience changed on rename\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_TOPIC_MESSAGES.audienceImmutable\", \"emittedBy\": \"apps/api/src/request-topics/request-topics.service.ts#updateTopic\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"unknown topic type on create\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_TOPIC_MESSAGES.typeUnknown\", \"emittedBy\": \"apps/api/src/request-topics/request-topics.service.ts#createTopic\", \"new\": true, \"note\": \"distinct object from the existing REQUEST_MESSAGES.typeUnknown ('Choose a request type') at index.ts:1841, which is spec 01's and stays\" },\n    { \"context\": \"missing topic name\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_TOPIC_MESSAGES.nameRequired\", \"emittedBy\": \"request-topics.service.ts#createTopic, #updateTopic\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"topic name over 60 characters\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_TOPIC_MESSAGES.nameTooLong\", \"emittedBy\": \"request-topics.service.ts#createTopic, #updateTopic\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"duplicate name in the audience\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_TOPIC_MESSAGES.nameDuplicate\", \"emittedBy\": \"request-topics.service.ts - mapped from Prisma P2002 on the functional unique index\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"caller lacks manage-request-topics\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_TOPIC_MESSAGES.manageForbidden\", \"emittedBy\": \"request-topics.service.ts on all four write routes\", \"new\": true, \"note\": \"cannot come from CapabilityGuard, whose message is fixed - see finding P5\" },\n    { \"context\": \"archive or restore into the status already held\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_TOPIC_MESSAGES.statusUnchanged\", \"emittedBy\": \"request-topics.service.ts#archiveTopic, #restoreTopic\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"the picker has no active topic\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_TOPIC_MESSAGES.pickerEmpty\", \"emittedBy\": \"no route - screen copy, apps/web/app/org/[orgId]/requests/NewRequestModal.tsx\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"no topicId on create\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_MESSAGES.topicRequired\", \"emittedBy\": \"apps/api/src/requests/requests.service.ts#createRequest\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"archived, foreign or unknown topicId on create\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_MESSAGES.topicUnavailable\", \"emittedBy\": \"apps/api/src/requests/requests.service.ts#createRequest\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"client-audience topic against a member addressee\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_MESSAGES.topicAudienceMismatch\", \"emittedBy\": \"apps/api/src/requests/requests.service.ts#createRequest\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"body carries type or accessKind\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_MESSAGES.classifierNotAccepted\", \"emittedBy\": \"apps/api/src/requests/requests.service.ts#createRequest via validateNewRequest\", \"new\": true },\n    { \"context\": \"topicId sent to PATCH .../requests/{id}\", \"module\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts#REQUEST_MESSAGES.fieldImmutable (index.ts:1865, exists)\", \"emittedBy\": \"apps/api/src/requests/requests.service.ts#patchRequest via validateRequestEdit (packages/validation/src/requests.ts:388)\", \"new\": false },\n    { \"context\": \"create and scope refusals on the requests routes\", \"module\": \"REQUEST_MESSAGES.createForbidden (index.ts:1839), REQUEST_MESSAGES.scopeForbidden (index.ts:1840), REQUEST_MESSAGES.editForbidden (index.ts:1864)\", \"emittedBy\": \"apps/api/src/requests/requests.service.ts:307, :175, :608 - all three already emit exactly these\", \"new\": false }\n  ],\n\n  \"premises\": [\n    { \"claim\": \"the migration runs before the services are rolled out, so the previous code serves against the new schema\", \"verifiedAt\": \"infra/deploy.sh:183-184 (infra/migrate.sh, one-off task from the new image) then infra/deploy.sh:187-188 (tf apply)\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"a functional UNIQUE index on LOWER(name) is how per-organization case-insensitive uniqueness is already done\", \"verifiedAt\": \"apps/api/prisma/migrations/20260901120000_spec_org_01_clients/migration.sql:30; also Project (20260827145447), BoardColumn and TaskLabel\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"POST .../requests today accepts and requires type, and accessKind when type is access\", \"verifiedAt\": \"packages/validation/src/requests.ts#validateNewRequest (requests.ts:294) via validateRequestKind; apps/api/src/requests/requests.service.ts:362-363 writes both\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"the callers that break by design are apps/api/test/requests.spec.ts, e2e/tests/requests.spec.ts and apps/web/.../NewRequestModal.tsx\", \"verifiedAt\": \"apps/api/test/requests.spec.ts:157,293,388,401; e2e/tests/requests.spec.ts:109,210,277,284; apps/web/app/org/[orgId]/requests/NewRequestModal.tsx:176-177,277,293 - and packages/validation/src/requests.test.ts:332-360, which the spec's blast radius does not name\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"the status words live in STATUS_OPTIONS (requests/page.tsx) and REQUEST_STATUS_META (RequestRow.tsx) and nowhere else\", \"verifiedAt\": \"apps/web/app/org/[orgId]/requests/page.tsx:35, RequestRow.tsx:8, and [requestId]/page.tsx:18 which imports REQUEST_STATUS_META from RequestRow - three surfaces, two definitions\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"signup is the only place an Organization is created\", \"verifiedAt\": \"apps/api/src/signup/signup.service.ts:46 - the only match for organization.create across apps/api/src, apps/api/test, e2e and scripts\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"REQUEST_MESSAGES is extended in place and none of the four new keys collides\", \"verifiedAt\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts:1807-1870 - topicRequired, topicUnavailable, topicAudienceMismatch and classifierNotAccepted are absent\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"a capability must be registered in both unions\", \"verifiedAt\": \"packages/validation/src/index.ts:506 (MemberCapability) and :613 (CAPABILITY_MATRIX, keyed by role so a new member fails compilation until all four roles are revisited); packages/validation/src/roles.ts:51 (Capability) and :108 (ROLE_CAPABILITIES)\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"cross-organization access on a guarded route answers 404\", \"verifiedAt\": \"apps/api/src/auth/org-scope.guard.ts:20-22, exercised by apps/api/test/org-scope.spec.ts\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"the e2e helpers the Verification Plan names all exist\", \"verifiedAt\": \"e2e/tests/helpers.ts:160 setMembershipRole, :734 signupOrg, :921 inviteAndAcceptViaApi\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"integration tests can observe columns the API does not return\", \"verifiedAt\": \"apps/api/test/holidays.spec.ts:10 imports PrismaService and :48 reads a membership row directly - which is how TC-02-INT-01's createdByAccountId and TC-02-INT-08's archivedAt are checked, since the documented topic row shape carries neither\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"REFUTED - 'an organization that predates the topics migration' is reachable in the integration harness\", \"verifiedAt\": \"apps/api/test/global-setup.ts:28 runs prisma migrate deploy before the suite and apps/api/jest.config.js declares it as globalSetup, so every migration is applied before any test body runs. See finding P2\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"REFUTED - CapabilityGuard can carry this spec's 403 message\", \"verifiedAt\": \"apps/api/src/auth/capability.guard.ts:63-66 throws a fixed body reading packages/validation/src/documents.ts:125, 'You do not have permission to manage templates'. See finding P5\" },\n    { \"claim\": \"PARTIAL - the pipeline's plan-coverage gate can see this spec\", \"verifiedAt\": \"scripts/handoff-coverage.mjs:70 matches numbered requirements as /^(\\\\d+)\\\\. /m and :85 matches cases as /^### (TC-...)/m in run.spec ALONE. This spec numbers its requirements as '#### REQ-02-001' headings and keeps every case in 02-request-topics.cases.md, so the gate reports 0/0 requirements and 0/0 cases and only the main file's eight ## headings are checked. The gate is not a witness for this spec; the sections map above answers for all three files by hand\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"doubleBehaviours\": [],\n\n  \"dsGaps\": [\n    { \"missing\": \"a reorder / drag-handle list primitive\", \"resolution\": \"ships as up and down controls on each row per the spec's DS gaps table, each keyboard-reachable and pointer-independent; recorded for a SortableList in @ds with a keyboard contract. BLOCKED: the spec does not say what a single press writes - see finding P1\" },\n    { \"missing\": \"a segmented-control primitive for the Staff / Client switch\", \"resolution\": \"ships as two @ds Buttons with aria-pressed, tokens only; recorded for a SegmentedControl in @ds adopted by this screen and the requests scope toggle together. Note: the identical ( Mine | All ) affordance on the screen this spec amends is drawn today with @ds Tabs (apps/web/app/org/[orgId]/requests/page.tsx:321-331), so the two audience-shaped switches will render differently until the primitive lands\" }\n  ],\n\n  \"risks\": [\n    { \"risk\": \"Retiring type and accessKind from the create body breaks four test files at once, three of which the blast radius names and one of which it does not (packages/validation/src/requests.test.ts:332-360).\", \"mitigation\": \"T8 rewrites all four; the unit file is listed in T1's files so the compilation break is found in the second the suite takes, not in an integration run.\" },\n    { \"risk\": \"The plan-coverage gate is blind to this spec's format and to its bundle members, so a dropped requirement or case would pass it silently.\", \"mitigation\": \"the sections map and testCases above were compiled by reading all three files; the gate's own limitation is recorded in premises so the next reader does not mistake a green run for coverage.\" },\n    { \"risk\": \"Seeded topic names ('Question', 'Other') are ordinary rows an organization may rename or archive, so no code may look one up by name.\", \"mitigation\": \"every read is by id; the seed list is a constant used once at signup and once in the migration, and is never re-applied.\" },\n    { \"risk\": \"The archived-topic marker on the request detail has no test id of its own and is asserted through request-detail-topic.\", \"mitigation\": \"the marker is rendered inside that element, so the E2E-03 assertion has something to read.\" },\n    { \"risk\": \"GET .../request-topics with an unrecognised status value has no stated behaviour (finding P4), while the sibling audience parameter is a stated 400.\", \"mitigation\": \"none available in the plan - a person decides.\" }\n  ]\n}\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
