{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cefx6nY1ykT8WdqT7pCfU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verdict: `blocked`.** The spec very nearly compiles — the plan is written and complete (8 tasks, 30/30 requirements assigned, 33/33 cases claimed, 22/22 sections accounted, 27/27 testids carried) — but two defects stop it and three more want a decision.\n\n**Blockers**\n\n- **P1 — the reorder contradicts itself.** Known Gaps says a reorder \"rewrites the affected rows in one transaction\"; DS gaps says each control issues \"one `PATCH`\"; the Routes table publishes exactly one single-row write. No implementation satisfies all three, and nothing says what the up control *sends* — client-computed `79` versus a server-side swap are both spec-conformant and differ in whether two curators can collide and whether two topics can end up sharing a `sortOrder`. `reorder` appears in the permission matrix, the actor table and the state machine, and in **no** numbered requirement and **no** case.\n- **P2 — TC-02-INT-02 needs a state the harness cannot produce.** It is AC-2's only observer and asks for an organization created *before* the migration, then for the test to run the migration. `apps/api/test/global-setup.ts:28` runs `prisma migrate deploy` before any test body, and workers 2..N are template copies of the migrated database. The two workarounds an author would reach for diverge: pasting a copy of the backfill SQL into the test passes while the shipped migration is wrong.\n\n**Lesser** — P3: the amended list wireframe drops the Type filter that REQ-02-003's rationale rests on, which decides whether the vacation section keeps its only selector (`requests-type-filter` is live at `page.tsx:338`, pinned by `requests.spec.ts:1294`). P4: unknown `?status=` value unstated while the sibling `audience` is an explicit 400. P5: the Guards column names `ManageRequestTopics`, but `CapabilityGuard` emits a fixed \"…manage templates\" body, so the required `manageForbidden` cannot come from it — the plan routes the check into the service, as holidays and requests already do.\n\n**One thing worth knowing beyond this spec:** `scripts/handoff-coverage.mjs` **passes** on this handoff and the pass is worthless — it reports `requirements 0/0 cases 0/0 sections 8/8`. It matches requirements as `^\\d+\\. ` while this spec uses `#### REQ-02-001` headings, and matches cases in `run.spec` alone while all 33 live in the `.cases.md` bundle member. For a bundled spec in this format the gate that exists to stop a plan dropping the hard part is blind to both. The counts above were compiled by hand."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":750,"cache_read_input_tokens":162916,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":750},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d8104197-4eeb-4137-8f54-59290205c2a9","uuid":"ba2df8c5-9bcb-44fe-a95f-dcc24c5c089f","timestamp":"2026-09-03T05:26:18.472Z","request_id":"req_011Cefx6mAv5HhDG7FM5WSr4"}
